# helm — Debian/Ubuntu source control.
#
# Target: Ubuntu 24.04 LTS and newer (ARCHITECTURE.md §5). Every package name
# below was checked against noble's own apt lists on 2026-08-26; where something
# is not in the archive it says so rather than pretending.
#
# NEEDS-HUMAN (maintainer identity): the Maintainer field must be a real,
# reachable address before anything is uploaded anywhere. It currently uses the
# RFC 2606 reserved `.invalid` domain so it cannot silently deliver to a
# stranger. Options: a project mailing list, a maintainers@ alias on a domain we
# own, or a named individual. Same decision blocks debian/changelog.
#
# NEEDS-HUMAN (hosting): no repository URL is invented here. Options: a Launchpad
# PPA (native fit for Ubuntu, needs a Launchpad account and a signing key), a
# self-hosted apt repo behind reprepro/aptly, or GitHub Releases with .deb
# artifacts and no apt metadata. Until this is decided, the only supported route
# is "build it yourself" — see docs/INSTALL.md.
Source: helm
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: helm contributors <helm-maintainers@helm.invalid>
# Ubuntu 24.04 ships rustc/cargo 1.75, which is below helm's declared MSRV of
# 1.82 (Cargo.toml). noble-updates carries versioned rustc-1.82/cargo-1.82
# packages (verified present), so those are named first and debian/rules puts
# the versioned toolchain on PATH.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               cargo-1.82 | cargo (>= 1.82),
               rustc-1.82 | rustc (>= 1.82),
               pkg-config
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/pipeliner/realms-de
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: helm
Architecture: any
# helm-river is the vendored, pinned river 0.4.x described in debian/rules.
# Plain `river` is offered as an alternative for distributions that ship 0.4.x
# themselves; Ubuntu 24.04 ships no river at all (verified), so on noble the
# vendored package is the only option.
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         helm-river (>= 0.4.0) | river (>= 0.4.0),
         dbus-user-session,
         systemd,
         xdg-desktop-portal,
         xdg-desktop-portal-gtk | xdg-desktop-portal-wlr | xdg-desktop-portal-gnome,
         fonts-symbola,
         foot,
         fuzzel,
         btop,
         zsh
# fonts-ibm-plex is the design's typeface but lives in multiverse, which is not
# enabled everywhere; a hard dependency would make helm uninstallable on a
# main+universe box. The glyph probe (ADR 0012) degrades to the system mono
# font instead of drawing tofu, so this is a Recommends and the install docs
# say how to get the real face.
Recommends: fonts-ibm-plex,
            gsettings-desktop-schemas,
            xwayland,
            xdg-desktop-portal-wlr
# Neither yazi nor starship is in the Ubuntu 24.04 archive (verified). charon
# and thoth are therefore degraded, not broken, on a stock noble box:
# docs/INSTALL.md says how to install them by hand.
Suggests: yazi,
          starship
Description: keyboard-first, gapless-tiling Wayland desktop environment
 helm is a Wayland desktop built around one idea: an ordered ledger of windows
 is the only state that matters, and every layout is a pure projection of it.
 Undo is exact, focus never moves a rectangle, and nothing animates.
 .
 It reuses proven tools rather than rewriting them — yazi, btop, zsh with
 starship, fuzzel and foot — and themes all of them from a single palette file.
 The compositor is river 0.4, driven by helm's own window manager over
 river-window-management-v1.
 .
 THIS PACKAGE IS PRE-ALPHA (0.1.0) AND DOES NOT INSTALL A WORKING DESKTOP.
 helm's binaries — the window manager, the bar, the CLI — are not written yet.
 What it installs today is the session contract: the wayland-session entry, the
 session wrapper that performs the systemd/D-Bus environment handshake, the
 systemd user units and the palette. Logging into it gives you river with no
 window management attached. See /usr/share/doc/helm/README.Debian and
 docs/INSTALL.md.
